<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Shindongbang buys 35,000T U.S. soybean.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Shindongbang buys 35,000T U.S. soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shindongbang Corp, South Korea's largest edible oil producer, bought 35,000 tonnes of U.S. No 2 soybean at a basis price over May futures on the Chicago Board of Trade, a senior company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The official said shipment was set for the end of April from the U.S. Gulf. Arrival was slated for the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>He said the purchase was equivalent to around $350 per tonne, C&amp;F, from a U.S. grain exporter.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
